  "Question": "Given that the ratio of \\(3x-4\\) to \\(y+15\\) is constant, and \\(y=3\\) when \\(x=2,\\) then, when \\(y=12,\\) \\(x\\) equals:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac18\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac87\\)",
    "C": "\\(\\dfrac73\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac72\\)",
    "E": "\\(8\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "First use the known values to find the constant ratio:\n\\[\n\\frac{3x-4}{y+15}\n=\\frac{3\\cdot2-4}{3+15}\n=\\frac2{18}=\\frac19.\n\\]\nWhen \\(y=12\\), the denominator is \\(27\\), so\n\\[\n\\frac{3x-4}{27}=\\frac19.\n\\]\nMultiplying by \\(27\\) gives \\(3x-4=3\\). Therefore \\(3x=7\\), and \\(\\boxed{x=\\dfrac73}\\), choice \\(\\mathrm C\\).",
